WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: ar

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Transcriber: Ghadir Atwi
المدقّق: Rana Al kilaney

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.099
Hello

00:00:20.099 --> 00:00:21.184
Hope you’re doing well

00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:23.603
My name is Nidal Ghaith

00:00:23.644 --> 00:00:25.980
Today I want to tell you a story

00:00:26.147 --> 00:00:28.357
I hope it inspires you

00:00:28.399 --> 00:00:31.903
and grant people patience and endurance

00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:33.780
and I hope you like my performance

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.531
God bless you

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.329
This happened 10 years ago or more

00:00:42.622 --> 00:00:45.374
I was at home one night

00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:47.960
My phone rang at 5:00 am

00:00:48.669 --> 00:00:51.339
It was a call from Germany

00:00:52.131 --> 00:00:53.758
My wife was studying in Germany

00:00:53.758 --> 00:00:56.844
She and my son were there

00:00:56.886 --> 00:00:58.096
The number was anonymous

00:00:58.096 --> 00:00:59.764
I answered

00:01:02.558 --> 00:01:07.647
It was the phone call that changed my life
as well as other people’s lives

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:11.192
My little family that I longed for

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:17.198
My world, my ambition, and everything
I aspired for to live a happy life

00:01:17.198 --> 00:01:22.203
Everything was about to collapse
because of this phone call

00:01:23.246 --> 00:01:29.460
They told me that my 10-month-old son
was suffering in the hospital

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.549
Yes, the hospital and that I had to
be there in no time

00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:43.558
I was an ambitious young man, just married
and it was my first baby

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.104
It was a very big shock for me

00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:52.066
For no reason, I had told my wife before

00:01:52.108 --> 00:01:56.696
,that if something happened to Abboud
I wouldn’t know how I would feel

00:01:58.781 --> 00:02:01.450
I was very confused and disappointed

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:03.202
I didn’t know what to do

00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:10.334
I grabbed whatever money I had at home
and took a car

00:02:10.585 --> 00:02:14.422
I only took my phone and charger with me

00:02:14.422 --> 00:02:18.259
and went to the airport

00:02:18.551 --> 00:02:24.056
I wanted to arrive but didn’t want to see
my son sick in hospital

00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:30.229
...I arrived to
On my way I booked a ticket

00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:33.774
I headed to the airport
and when I arrived

00:02:34.192 --> 00:02:37.195
The place was full of security officers

00:02:37.195 --> 00:02:42.450
?Why me? Why did they choose me
?Why don’t you carry any luggage with you

00:02:46.871 --> 00:02:50.833
?Why are you travelling in such a way
My son, was the answer

00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:55.004
I was crying. I told them that my son
was in critical condition at the hospital

00:02:59.217 --> 00:03:01.344
and inspection took more time 
than expected

00:03:01.344 --> 00:03:03.429
Rather than questioning me for 10 minutes

00:03:03.429 --> 00:03:08.851
They spent a long time
until I boarded the plane

00:03:08.851 --> 00:03:15.441
Five hours passed as if they were
thirty years. During this time

00:03:15.441 --> 00:03:17.860
I thought everything was only a dream

00:03:21.364 --> 00:03:22.365
It’s impossible

00:03:22.365 --> 00:03:23.407
My life is different

00:03:23.658 --> 00:03:29.330
What’s going on? Why is it 
?changing? Is it reality

00:03:30.456 --> 00:03:33.334
I only thought it was a
dream that would end soon

00:03:34.001 --> 00:03:38.089
After 5 hours, the plane
finally landed in Dusseldorf’s airport

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:40.341
I arrived and found... I found

00:03:40.466 --> 00:03:42.760
two Palestinian students waiting for me

00:03:44.303 --> 00:03:45.304
So it wasn’t a dream

00:03:46.264 --> 00:03:50.101
This means everything is real
the things

00:03:50.101 --> 00:03:53.896
Everything was real

00:03:53.938 --> 00:03:57.858
This dream won’t end
they took me to the hospital by car

00:03:58.234 --> 00:04:02.947
We arrived to University Hospital of
Dusseldorf Center for Pediatrics

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:07.576
I went through a crowd of Palestinian
students who were standing at the door

00:04:07.827 --> 00:04:09.161
Coming to console my wife

00:04:09.287 --> 00:04:11.706
Consolation meant a critical condition

00:04:11.706 --> 00:04:18.421
A healthy kid in a critical health
condition... suddenly

00:04:20.006 --> 00:04:23.718
.I entered. They gave me a mask to wear
Same procedures we apply today

00:04:27.388 --> 00:04:31.434
.I wore a uniform too and entered
,When I looked in front of me

00:04:33.269 --> 00:04:36.981
I saw my happy little son whom I was
playing with two weeks ago

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:46.532
.I saw a piece of flesh
His body was black

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.744
I didn’t believe my eyes

00:04:49.827 --> 00:04:56.125
.I was still hoping it was a dream
I wished it had been a dream

00:04:56.125 --> 00:04:59.920
I wished to wake up from that nightmare

00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:06.761
I couldn’t handle it. All the energy
in me. All the energy in my heart

00:05:06.886 --> 00:05:11.557
...that I had collected and watched
piling them up like pebbles

00:05:11.557 --> 00:05:13.726
burst out from my chest

00:05:14.018 --> 00:05:15.144
I sat down watching him

00:05:16.896 --> 00:05:23.694
.He was on his death bed
No signs of life were on his black body

00:05:23.694 --> 00:05:30.618
I couldn’t withstand it so I left the room
to find my wife. I hugged her

00:05:32.286 --> 00:05:39.293
She unconsciously told me that If we lost
him, she would bring me ten sons instead

00:05:41.754 --> 00:05:42.755
She was lying

00:05:48.511 --> 00:05:55.476
The German doctor approached ignoring
the mother and father’s feelings

00:05:59.063 --> 00:06:01.899
?Where did they get him from

00:06:04.527 --> 00:06:11.450
He might die. Nobody overcomes this 
illness. The probability of staying alive

00:06:13.494 --> 00:06:20.501
was very low. I wished the dream
would end. I wished everything

00:06:21.085 --> 00:06:22.086
were a dream

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:25.172
O people. This is impossible
I was dreaming yesterday

00:06:25.172 --> 00:06:26.924
We fight and fight to live

00:06:27.383 --> 00:06:29.260
and now we’re knocking death’s door

00:06:32.096 --> 00:06:37.560
.The doctor was void of feelings
He didn’t sympathize with us at all

00:06:39.353 --> 00:06:40.354
I

00:06:41.647 --> 00:06:47.445
.didn’t take his words into account
I believed in one only thing. This child

00:06:49.655 --> 00:06:53.534
is the child of all Palestinians

00:06:55.327 --> 00:06:56.579
who all

00:06:57.872 --> 00:06:59.331
fight for life

00:06:59.874 --> 00:07:06.881
I was sure he could do it. They said
he’d die and I was sure he’d survive

00:07:09.383 --> 00:07:16.348
They were 36 hours. If everything went
fine, he may peacefully live

00:07:18.225 --> 00:07:21.270
His body temperature was more than
forty-two degrees celsius

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:28.068
His heartbeats were highly pulsing
All his internal organs malfunctioned

00:07:28.903 --> 00:07:34.325
Liver, kidneys, everything inside his
stomach stopped working

00:07:34.325 --> 00:07:35.326
Nothing was working

00:07:36.076 --> 00:07:37.995
The first 36 hours passed

00:07:38.329 --> 00:07:42.458
and the doctor was sure he was in a 
dangerous condition

00:07:43.334 --> 00:07:44.877
We know how he will survive

00:07:45.586 --> 00:07:47.421
We don’t know how he will live

00:07:47.963 --> 00:07:48.964
Maybe blind

00:07:50.174 --> 00:07:51.175
Maybe deaf

00:07:51.509 --> 00:07:53.052
He may lose learning abilities

00:07:53.636 --> 00:07:54.845
He may live with no limbs

00:07:55.763 --> 00:07:56.972
He may live as a human

00:07:58.182 --> 00:08:00.392
but like a body only

00:08:03.854 --> 00:08:09.902
Nobody can bear this
It’s very hard. He might die

00:08:09.985 --> 00:08:10.986
in front of you

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:22.581
.Twelve days passed
Medical delegations coming and going

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:29.296
.We were hoping to hear good news
We weren’t able to see what was going on

00:08:29.296 --> 00:08:36.220
Did we want to see a corpse, or signs 
of death on the skin, or dried fingers

00:08:36.679 --> 00:08:39.014
or cirrhosis of body organs

00:08:39.515 --> 00:08:44.311
Nothing was working but our faith
in Allah (God) was strong

00:08:45.396 --> 00:08:52.069
We were sure our son would fight till the
last breath, even though he was a baby

00:08:52.069 --> 00:08:59.076
because he wanted to survive, we were
patiently waiting at the door

00:09:00.202 --> 00:09:04.290
After 12 days, a nurse came out

00:09:05.165 --> 00:09:08.877
I still remember like it was yesterday

00:09:09.837 --> 00:09:16.760
.She said our hero responded to treatment
We will transfer him to

00:09:17.886 --> 00:09:18.887
the second hospital

00:09:20.764 --> 00:09:22.474
To us, this was the critical part

00:09:25.769 --> 00:09:32.109
They carried him in a helicopter
along with 5 doctors

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:36.280
I still remember it was yellow and small

00:09:36.864 --> 00:09:39.700
...It flew up high and away

00:09:41.327 --> 00:09:45.247
.We are in our city and we know no one
?How about moving to another city

00:09:45.247 --> 00:09:49.376
Moving to a faraway city. We
don’t even know Iraq

00:09:49.376 --> 00:09:53.380
I delegated my command to Allah

00:09:55.466 --> 00:10:01.597
?Why this examination
?Why all of this patience

00:10:01.597 --> 00:10:04.850
Thinking in the train. Moving
between cities

00:10:05.517 --> 00:10:11.023
.Thinking about my son
?How will his life be

00:10:15.319 --> 00:10:21.241
?How will he feel
?How will people accept him

00:10:25.204 --> 00:10:28.832
We were a family whose son was
.between life and death

00:10:31.502 --> 00:10:35.130
Ideas were flooding in. Finally, we
arrived to Mannheim city

00:10:36.382 --> 00:10:43.305
.At the hospital, we met the doctors
Sign the documents

00:10:44.264 --> 00:10:47.393
Here, stamp. We finished all procedures

00:10:47.643 --> 00:10:49.853
We had to wait for 2-3 days

00:10:49.853 --> 00:10:50.896
for the surgery

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.196
After 12 hours

00:11:00.614 --> 00:11:02.908
they called us from the hospital

00:11:04.243 --> 00:11:06.036
Hello, be at the hospital now

00:11:07.621 --> 00:11:13.377
Another surgery is recommended. They 
performed one 2-3 days ago

00:11:17.256 --> 00:11:21.635
.We started to run crazily 
We ran until we reached the hospital

00:11:21.635 --> 00:11:28.142
In Germany, operation rooms
are underground. We met the doctor

00:11:28.767 --> 00:11:35.774
He told us that they would perform another
surgery. Please stay outside

00:11:37.735 --> 00:11:38.736
It required 5 hours

00:11:39.695 --> 00:11:43.365
That surgery was necessary otherwise
he would die

00:11:46.577 --> 00:11:51.623
After 2 hours, the doctor called us. He
asked us to meet him quickly

00:11:52.916 --> 00:11:59.798
We left everything and ran to the hospital

00:12:00.174 --> 00:12:03.093
We arrived to the clinic’s door

00:12:03.218 --> 00:12:05.763
.The doctor showed up 
He didn’t die, he shouted

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:14.813
You must take a decision. We
diagnosed his limbs. They’re lifeless

00:12:17.316 --> 00:12:18.317
They’re just dead

00:12:19.193 --> 00:12:23.864
So you either choose to amputate
his limbs

00:12:25.032 --> 00:12:27.534
Or he’d die in 2 to 3 days

00:12:30.621 --> 00:12:32.790
This decision was harder than death itself

00:12:33.665 --> 00:12:36.126
This thing is harder than death

00:12:36.418 --> 00:12:39.463
Death is easier

00:12:39.463 --> 00:12:40.714
It’s easier

00:12:44.885 --> 00:12:50.682
I remember myself running back and forth
the hospital until I gathered my strength

00:12:50.682 --> 00:12:51.975
and went to the doctor

00:12:53.727 --> 00:13:00.651
,I told him, I accept, a lump of flesh 
blind, I agree, deaf, it’s fine

00:13:02.194 --> 00:13:09.117
.Without limbs, I give up. I surrendered
I only wanted my son to survive

00:13:10.994 --> 00:13:17.459
His shape never mattered anymore. His
abilities... It’s fine

00:13:19.962 --> 00:13:23.006
We took the decision to amputate his limbs

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:31.056
The surgery was over after 2 hours. I
saw the child in front of me

00:13:31.056 --> 00:13:33.475
with no limbs

00:13:35.269 --> 00:13:38.021
They cut off two legs in the first surgery

00:13:38.313 --> 00:13:45.320
It was weird to see your 10-month-old son
disabled

00:13:48.907 --> 00:13:53.787
You’ll stop thinking about your days or
about your life, you’ll think of his life

00:13:53.787 --> 00:13:56.498
He’ll live in a different way

00:13:59.751 --> 00:14:01.920
Nobody could withstand the scene

00:14:02.212 --> 00:14:05.132
The heart can’t bear such a feeling

00:14:07.134 --> 00:14:09.845
Thirty six surgeries

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:13.974
Amputating the four limbs

00:14:15.225 --> 00:14:21.982
Transplanting new skin just pulling it
from the head and after 2 weeks

00:14:26.737 --> 00:14:30.616
transplanting another. They changed

00:14:31.783 --> 00:14:34.369
everything. Our happiness was limitless

00:14:35.162 --> 00:14:42.127
when he opened his eyes and saw his
bottle of milk. He followed it by the eyes

00:14:44.129 --> 00:14:46.548
We felt overjoyed

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:49.217
.He could see
.He was looking around

00:14:49.885 --> 00:14:51.053
We were thankful

00:14:51.136 --> 00:14:53.305
This is very important to us

00:14:53.347 --> 00:14:54.348
He could see

00:14:54.932 --> 00:14:59.519
He had no limbs, but he could hear

00:15:00.979 --> 00:15:01.980
No limbs. It’s okay

00:15:02.689 --> 00:15:04.107
Thanks God he’s alive

00:15:05.317 --> 00:15:06.318
He survived

00:15:07.486 --> 00:15:14.368
They were 5 months of severe torture

00:15:15.285 --> 00:15:18.080
My wife played an important role

00:15:19.247 --> 00:15:23.168
My wife was a patient woman. Very patient

00:15:23.752 --> 00:15:24.795
She gave me strength

00:15:25.003 --> 00:15:31.843
.After 5 months, we decided to leave 
Abboud’s limbs were cut off

00:15:34.638 --> 00:15:37.182
and he received intensive care

00:15:39.059 --> 00:15:45.899
We either had to live in Germany or leave
back to our country. We decided to leave

00:15:47.234 --> 00:15:48.485
Better die in Al-Quds

00:15:48.568 --> 00:15:55.575
The stones of Al-Quds will give us the 
support we need to persist. We will be

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:03.583
between our beloved. They will provide us
with love and support

00:16:05.335 --> 00:16:10.007
.Our country will support us
We will feel rooted

00:16:11.508 --> 00:16:18.515
We decided to leave with a different child
who looks incomplete but

00:16:19.933 --> 00:16:23.895
is complete with his mind, perseverance
and determination

00:16:24.396 --> 00:16:27.190
Now, let me introduce Abboud to you

00:17:01.058 --> 00:17:07.022
Even though he is disabled, he isn’t
...different. Here you go Abboud

00:17:07.564 --> 00:17:13.779
Hello, I’m Abdelatif Ghaith, a determined 
challenger, and up to the challenge

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:38.845
Abboud is fully integrated. He’s 
different by shape, but similar by heart

00:17:38.845 --> 00:17:45.685
He goes to an ordinary school and dreams
about a good life. This is our message to

00:17:53.819 --> 00:17:54.820
all challengers

00:17:57.447 --> 00:18:00.075
They are an integral part of our society

00:18:01.284 --> 00:18:03.120
Everyone must treat them well

00:18:06.206 --> 00:18:07.207
Thank you all

00:18:09.417 --> 00:18:11.545
Yes, she’s here

00:18:38.697 --> 00:18:45.495
Thank you for your feelings. The message 
is from Allah. He chose us on purpose

00:18:45.662 --> 00:18:51.376
We are a conservative family and I took
great care of my eldest son. When I was

00:18:55.755 --> 00:19:02.762
studying in Germany, I devoted my life to 
my son. I took great care of him

00:19:07.934 --> 00:19:11.438
This is our fate

00:19:12.731 --> 00:19:19.613
The message was from Allah. He wanted us 
to carry such a responsibility

00:19:20.822 --> 00:19:21.823
and be reliable

00:19:22.824 --> 00:19:24.284
Thanks to Allah

00:19:24.284 --> 00:19:28.872
we’re working on Abboudi’s abilities
to be a role model

00:19:28.872 --> 00:19:32.834
for many people

00:19:32.918 --> 00:19:39.925
Many people tell us that we’ve touched
their lives. They want to start

00:19:41.593 --> 00:19:48.433
.We must be an idol for others
We must keep going

00:19:49.559 --> 00:19:56.399
Abboud will grow up normally as any other
kid. You’ll see

00:20:02.572 --> 00:20:09.496
in all societies, especially Al-Quds
which is our goal

00:20:13.583 --> 00:20:14.584
Thank you so much

00:20:19.714 --> 00:20:20.715
Let’s go

